                <pb facs="1052" n="936" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg936"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.51 Et 3/15: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bading</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-01T12:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 10:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>19. Your 17, November 6, 3 p.m. In view of the general opinion that the loan will
                    be a failure and that the final contract will not be signed, I have not thought
                    it desirable to bring the matter to the President’s attention unless again
                    instructed to do so by the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bading</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
